TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_BS_UnityThroughStrength=Applying Force
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_BS_UnityThroughStrength=We secure our interests using military force. 
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_BS_UnityThroughStrength=Strength is of course the most obvious tool in our geopolitical toolbox, but that doesn't make it any less effective. Our researchers have developed better tools and methodology to exploit the martial potential of the nations we have interests in. 

TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_BS_RootingOutCorruption=Rooting Out Corruption
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_BS_RootingOutCorruption=We improve the administration of our nations.
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_BS_RootingOutCorruption=Until now, we have tolerated a certain amount of graft to secure the support of key individuals and organizations, but these petty interests now stand in the way of our goals. We have developed specific plans to reduce the influence of these actors, or where necessary, completely remove them from the picture.

TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_BS_SecuringOurInterests=A New Status Quo
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_BS_SecuringOurInterests=We stabilize our nations and make them more productive. 
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_BS_SecuringOurInterests=There were many guardrails dismantled to get where we are now. Guardrails that we now wish we had to maintain our grip on power. Alongside that, the enormous changes that we and others have brought about have left their mark on the collective psyche. Uncertainty is quietly killing our potential. We have begun implementing reforms designed to protect our intermediaries and restore trust.

TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_BS_ProprietarySpaceResearchI=Proprietary Space Research : Resources
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_BS_ProprietarySpaceResearchI=We determine how to extract resources from asteroids using existing technology. 
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_BS_ProprietarySpaceResearchI=It appears a foregone conclusion that humans will need to learn to exploit the abundance of resources in space. But right now, we lack many of the basic technologies we need to do that. Nevertheless, our researchers believe that there are options that would allow us to begin accumulating resources in the near term, albeit limited in scope, and at far lower yields. We have paved the way for extracting resources from nearby asteroids. However, other extraction targets pose unique engineering challenges that remain unaddressed.

TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_BS_ProprietarySpaceResearchII=Proprietary Space Research : Space Stations
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_BS_ProprietarySpaceResearchII=We determine how to build larger space stations using existing technology. 
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_BS_ProprietarySpaceResearchII=In theory, building larger space stations is primarily an issue of resources and labor, but in practice it comes with a whole host of new problems, resolution of which requires technologies that are either immature or still entirely theoretical. Still, our researchers have come up with some creative solutions that should allow us to expand our stations, though we will generally be limited to smaller, lower-population hab modules until more basic research has been completed. 

TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_BS_ProprietarySpaceResearchIII=Proprietary Space Research : Orbital Laboratories
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_BS_ProprietarySpaceResearchIII=We leverage our larger stations and space infrastucture to build advanced oribital laboraties. 
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_BS_ProprietarySpaceResearchIII=We have achieved much, but further progress now requires that we improve our research capabilities. To that end, our scientists and engineers have put forward some promising plans for improving our space-based research labs.  

